# The card image this version of the radio software wants, per radio: <model> <level> <what that image brings>.
# Raise a radio's level when a change reaches it only with a card image (the kernel, its modules such as the
# WiFi driver, U-Boot, the root filesystem's packages): the in-radio update cannot carry those. The image
# build (buildroot/local-build.sh) stamps the level into /etc/openx6x00-image, which no update touches;
# x6100-update and the GUI compare the two and say when a newer card image is worth writing. Images up to
# v0.3.3 have no stamp: level 1.
#
# A level that only the kernel (with its modules) and/or U-Boot bring gets a second line, <model>-boot <level>
# <parts>, parts being kernel and/or uboot: the release's own bundle carries them, and the radio installs them onto
# its SD card when ticked in the update question (x6100-update install --kernel/--uboot), which reaches that level
# without a card image. Each level from the card's own to the one wanted needs such a line, else a card image is
# still needed. Add one only in a release after the first whose updater reads it (the one after v0.3.12.18): an older
# updater installs the software alone and then says a card image is wanted.
#   x6200 3 the kernel 6.1.90 (a WiFi fix)
#   x6200-boot 3 kernel
x6100 3 the Internet radio's AAC, Ogg, Opus, FLAC and HLS stations (ffmpeg), and the WiFi driver fix (MediaTek and UniFi access points)
x6200 3 the Internet radio's AAC, Ogg, Opus, FLAC and HLS stations (ffmpeg), and the WiFi driver fix
